# What never belongs in the build context.
#
# Two different reasons are mixed here and both matter. Most entries are size:
# the context is tarred and sent to the daemon before the first instruction
# runs, and .git plus a local .venv is the bulk of this checkout. The entries
# under "credentials and runtime state" are not about size at all — `var/`
# holds the egress WireGuard configs (a PrivateKey each) and the payload
# store, and a `.env` holds the database URL. A file that reaches the context
# can reach a layer, and a layer is shipped.
#
# This file is a deny-list rather than an allow-list because the Dockerfile
# already copies by name (pyproject.toml, uv.lock, src/, migrations/, …) —
# nothing outside those lines is copied even when it survives this file.

# Version control and CI
.git/
.github/
.githooks/

# Credentials and runtime state. `**/` because a bare `.env` matches only at
# the context root, and the context *is* the repository root (the compose
# file builds with `context: ..`) while the documented deploy flow puts the
# real secrets in `deploy/.env`. Last match wins in this file, so the
# `.env.example` negation must stay after the exclusions it re-admits.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
var/
*.conf
*.pem
*.key
*.cookies.txt

# Local build and tool state — the image builds its own venv from uv.lock, and
# copying a host one in would put absolute host paths in the image.
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Not part of the runtime
tests/
docs/
decisions/
tool/
Justfile
*.md
!README.md

# Editor and OS junk
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
*.swp
